  "reason": "Evidence: The top-4 configurations all share scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer aggregation, with config_007 (vit_l, weighted) at 0.725 as the current best. The only untested configuration in this high-performing neighborhood is config_050 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat). While resnet50 has been slightly lower in accuracy than vit_l (0.713 vs 0.725), config_031 showed resnet50 can achieve a higher F1 (0.695 vs 0.685), suggesting it captures complementary signal. This experiment tests whether the transformer+concat fusion with resnet50 might produce a small accuracy gain or at least confirm the ceiling of the scvi_n200+transformer family. It is the best use of experiment 9 because it is the highest-expected-accuracy untested option remaining; all other untested configs either drop to avgpool or use weaker encoders (scgpt, pca). Expected relative cost: high (~6 GPU hours), comparable to config_031 (6.22 hrs), due to multiprofile transformer aggregation with resnet50. Since accuracy is the primary objective and we have one experiment remaining, investing in the most competitive architecture is justified."
